# Chroma library, modern Earth: SHAPE MOMENTS for the ladder shapes competition and venture (v25 prep, draft 10-23).
# Pours into chroma-library/earth_shape_moments-*.lib (POUR-NOTES.md). Nothing built or run.
# Layout: every moment is a life event in the balance layout: W U B R G once each, then one full cross cycle.
#   cycle A: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W       cycle B: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W       (13 moments each over this file)
# aim: tags as aims-shape.md section 4. Fork moments (plateau, cost, chance, round) also offer `ease` for "postpone or
# slow down", as the v25 decisions ask (V25-DECISIONS.md, Aims); check with the Engine that ease is read on cost,
# chance and round. arrive options carry no aim: tag.
# competition rungs 0-4 (taking part, regular, winning, master, summit); venture rungs 0-3 (first steps out, a seasoned
# hand, known for it, a legend of it). Competition moments open from 8 where children do it; venture from 14.

# ================================================================ COMPETITION

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- competition: practice, low rungs (cycle A)

== an ordinary night of {aim.doing}
tier: life event
shape: competition
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 8-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: leisure, friends
horizon: week
roles: friend, rival, mentor
earth: an ordinary evening of {aim.doing} at {aim.place}, the kind that adds up
tribal: an evening of {aim.doing} by the fire, the kind the elders say adds up
magic: an evening of {aim.doing} in the tower's long hall, the kind the masters say adds up
scene: It is an ordinary weeknight at {aim.place}, and nobody is watching. {N} has been {aim.doing} for an hour and one thing still will not come right. The first real date of the season is a month off, and the others are starting to pack up.
scene tribal: The fire is low and most of the clan is asleep. {N} is still at {aim.doing}, and one move will not come right, with the gathering of the clans a moon away.
scene magic: The tower's long hall is empty but for {N} and one stubborn lamp. One part of {aim.doing} still will not come right, and the masters' trial is a month off.
- W | finish the drill exactly as it was set, every last repeat | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 85
- U | go over the one thing slowly until you see why it goes wrong | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | ask the best one there for a lesson, and stay until it comes right | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- R | drop the drill and just mess about for the rest of the night | v: hedonism, stimulation | aim: ease | foot: lesson play keeps it alive | chance: 92
- G | stop when the body says stop, and come back fresh next week | v: security, tradition | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 90
- W>U | note down what went wrong, and set the same drill for next week | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson small notes add up | chance: 80
- U>B | work out which weakness the others will spot first, and fix that | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: door learned a skill | chance: 65
- B>R | turn the last half hour into a contest with whoever is left | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 75
- R>G | keep going with a friend long after it stops being practice | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 85
- G>W | help the newer ones set up, and walk home the long way | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 92
works: The thing that would not come right comes right near the end, almost by accident.
works: Nothing dramatic happens, and {N} goes home a little better at {aim.doing} than before.
fails: The one thing is still wrong at closing time, and {N} carries it home like a stone in a shoe.
fails: It is a flat night: tired hands, a wandering head, nothing learned that anyone could name.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- competition: practice, higher rungs (cycle B)

== the hours nobody sees
tier: life event
shape: competition
kind: practice
rungs: 2 3 4
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 10-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: leisure, body
horizon: months
roles: mentor, rival, friend
earth: the long, quiet training between the big dates, where the small gaps are closed or not
tribal: the long days of practice between the gatherings of the clans, when nobody comes to watch
magic: the long hours of drill between the court's great trials, in an empty yard at dawn
scene: At this level everyone at {aim.place} is good, and the gap between {N} and the very best is small and stubborn. The next big date is six weeks off, and the plan says the hard part starts now.
scene tribal: Everyone who still comes to the practice ground is strong now, and the gap between {N} and the best of the clan is a hand's width. The next gathering is six weeks off.
scene magic: Every pupil left in the yard is good, and the gap between {N} and the best of them is small and stubborn. The court's trial is six weeks off.
- W | keep to the plan to the letter, rest days included | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: mark kept your word | chance: 80
- U | take apart the last three defeats and find the pattern in them | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | add a second session every day, whatever it costs | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means time-.08 | chance: 65
- R | throw out the plan for a week and do it for joy alone | v: hedonism, stimulation | aim: ease | foot: lesson joy is part of the work | chance: 88
- G | ease off for a week and let the body catch up | v: security, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 90
- W>B | train to the group's schedule, and quietly outwork everyone in it | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 70
- B>G | cut everything that does not help, but keep one family day a week | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 72
- G>U | go back to the first teacher and relearn the basics properly | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- U>R | try a strange new approach for a month, just to see what breaks | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- R>W | turn the hardest session into a game the whole group plays | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 75
works: Somewhere in the second month the gap closes by a hair, and {N} feels it before anyone says so.
works: The work is dull and it holds: {N} comes out of the six weeks sharper than they went in.
fails: Six weeks of effort and the gap has not moved, and {N} cannot see why.
fails: The weeks blur together, and {N} arrives at the big date tired rather than ready.

