- U>B | learn everything {mentor} knows, and then where {mentor} is wrong | v: self-direction, power | aim: work | foot: lesson even teachers miss things | chance: 60
- B>R | ask for the hardest sessions going, and none of the easy ones | v: achievement, stimulation | aim: work | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 60
- R>G | go for the company as much as the teaching, and enjoy it | v: hedonism, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: person friend | chance: 88
- G>W | bring {parent} along, so the whole family agrees to it | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 82
works: {mentor} shows one small change, and a month later {N} cannot imagine doing it the old way.
works: Whatever {N} decided, {mentor} stays a friendly face at {aim.place}, and that counts for something.
fails: The advice is good but does not fit yet, and for a while {N} feels clumsier, not better.
fails: It takes longer to settle than anyone hoped, and {N} is caught between two ways of doing it.

