scene: To go on at this level, {aim.doing} now needs more: fees, travel to every {aim.contest}, better equipment and evenings that used to be the family's. Next season's money is due at the end of the month, and the household has started doing sums at the kitchen table.
scene tribal: To go on, {N} must walk to every gathering and give up hunting days the family counts on. The elders say the clan can carry it, but not for nothing.
scene magic: The guild's fees have doubled at this grade, and the journeys to the court are long. The household's steward has started doing sums by candlelight, and the fees are due at the month's end.
